            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sophie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this a great basic recipe. I like to play with recipes so I added some cinnamon and nutmeg . Also took dried tart cherries soaked in water then drained to recipe. Was very good . Topped with home made whipped cream. Yum yum. Thank you",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-13T20:09:07.843Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Umm, it struck me right away looking at this recipe that it's lacking any kind of spice. As written, it couldn't help but taste bland and boring. Just add some cinnamon (1/2 to 1 tsp.) and of course a good dash of nutmeg. I would never bother making it as written, but I did rate it for the way it was written. Add the spices and you will have a very nice bread pudding that easily goes up to five stars!",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-02T12:50:32.683Z"
          },
